Subject: [PATCH milos-linux v1 0/3] media: qcom: camss: Milos front camera (CSIPHY3) fixes
To: Jorijn van der Graaf <jorijnvdgraaf@catcrafts.net>

Three small fixes for the Milos CAMSS support in milos-linux
(combined-stable 63289f441152) that make the Fairphone 6 front camera
(S5KKD1 on CSIPHY3, D-PHY) stream:

1. drop the C-PHY per-rate entries from the D-PHY lane table,
2. widen the CSID-340 PHY select field to three bits (PHY3 + 1 = 4 was
   truncated to 0),
3. use 16-byte RDI line alignment for Milos (TFE 128-bit bus).

All three are based on the Fairphone camera-kernel sources
(670223e10713). Tested on the Fairphone 6: all three sensors (IMX896,
OV13B10, S5KKD1) capture with libcamera; rear strides are unchanged.

These target the milos-linux tree (not mainline, where Milos CAMSS is
not merged yet). They could also be squashed into the Milos CAMSS
patches before those are posted to linux-media.

Development was assisted by an AI coding tool (see the Assisted-by tags).

Paul Schuldesz (3):
  media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: Drop C-PHY rate settings from the
    Milos D-PHY table
  media: qcom: camss: csid-340: Use a three-bit PHY select field
  media: qcom: camss: vfe: Align Milos RDI lines to 16 bytes

